{"id": 92, "ts": 1783837412.921945, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "I acknowledge Sofia\u2019s points on Candidate\u202fB\u2019s proven stress resilience and conscientiousness, but I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fC is the stronger overall fit. While we lack concrete anecdotes of C\u2019s crew\u2011cooperation, the factual profile shows that C can anticipate dangerous situations, sees complex connections, and possesses excellent spatial vision\u2014abilities that directly support decision quality and situational awareness on long\u2011haul flights. Moreover, C\u2019s very good leadership qualities suggest the capacity to guide a crew through complex scenarios, even if the current notes flag a tendency to be a \u201cshow\u2011off\u201d and resistant to new ideas. In a safety\u2011critical cockpit, the ability to foresee hazards and understand intricate system interactions outweighs the more stylistic communication flaws observed in B, especially given B\u2019s documented nasty remarks toward colleagues, which pose a clear risk to crew harmony. Therefore, I continue to recommend Candidate\u202fC, pending any further evidence of his cooperation or adaptability."}
